;; =============================================================================
;; Spec: Ariadne step 2d — enforce grants on Kubernetes deploy
;; =============================================================================

{:spec/title "Require granted, transacted Kubernetes deployments"

 :spec/description
 "Finish the deployment half of Ariadne step 2d. Replace the direct
  kustomize-apply! path with a durable effect proposal, a narrowly scoped
  :effect/deploy grant, an allow-class DecisionEnvelope, commit-time authority
  recheck, and provider reconciliation.

  Reuse check-resource-count and check-gke-node-limit as policy inputs rather
  than duplicating deployment checks. Render the provider dry-run into the
  proposal before mutation. Preserve rollback evidence on failed and successful
  apply paths so partial mutations remain recoverable. Decompose the current
  nested deploy phase into provider, domain-decision, and application-flow
  namespaces before adding enforcement.

  PREFLIGHT BASIS — the reused checks are vacuous as written. Both parse Pulumi
  preview JSON (policy/parse-preview -> json/parse-string, exceptions swallowed
  to {}). Against a kustomize render they yield no steps and therefore no
  violations, so deploy-authority/preflight returns :allow for any manifest.
  Measured on main (1eab1888b): a 5000-document kustomize render returns
  {:preflight/result :allow :preflight/violations []}. deploy-governed/transact!
  does call both checks before the apply, so the previous acceptance criteria
  ('check-X is evaluated before the real apply') were satisfiable by a gate that
  cannot deny anything. Evaluation is not enforcement; the criteria below now
  require a demonstrated denial over a kustomize render.

  Kustomize is the primary Kubernetes provisioning path, so the checks become
  kustomize-aware rather than the deploy seam acquiring a separate basis. Two
  sub-decisions belong to this work, not to this spec: whether to add a YAML
  parser dependency (phase-deployment currently has cheshire and malli only, no
  YAML reader) or split documents structurally; and what check-gke-node-limit
  means over a kustomize render, given GKE node pools are infrastructure rather
  than manifest resources — either it counts NodePool kinds in the render, or it
  is explicitly scoped to the Pulumi path and deploy gains a second check that
  can fail against kustomize. Whichever is chosen, no check may be left in the
  preflight path unable to return a violation for the artifact it receives.

  PROVIDER SHAPE — deploy-provider does not yet satisfy the map transact!
  expects, and wiring it unreconciled introduces a second fail-open.
  transact! calls (:dry-run! provider) with one argument; deploy-provider/dry-run!
  is 2-arity ([{:keys [namespace context]} rendered-yaml]). commit! branches on
  (:deploy/failed? applied); deploy-provider/apply! returns a schema-shaped map
  ({:success? ...}) that has no :deploy/failed? key, so a failed apply reads
  falsy and never records :effect/outcome :failed. :observe! and :rollback-info!
  already match on both arity and return shape. The exact-bytes operations
  (render!, apply-rendered!, dry-run!) landed in #1713 for this purpose: the
  bytes recorded in the proposal must be the bytes applied, so :apply! binds to
  apply-rendered! over the captured render rather than re-running kustomize."

 :spec/intent
 {:type :feature
  :scope ["components/phase-deployment/**"]}

 :spec/constraints
 ["No kubectl mutation runs without an active matching grant and allow-class envelope"
  "The durable proposal is the authority recheck input at commit"
  "Existing deployment policy checks are reused rather than reimplemented"
  "Every check in the preflight path parses the artifact the configured provider actually renders"
  "A check that cannot return a violation for the render it receives is not left in the preflight path"
  "The bytes recorded in the durable proposal are the bytes applied — no re-render between dry-run and apply"
  "The dry-run output is durable before the real apply begins"
  "Rollback evidence survives every apply outcome"
  "Provider operations, domain decisions, and phase orchestration remain separate"
  "Repeated proposal, grant, and envelope maps use shared test factories"
  "Functions must express one decision or orchestration step without nested control pyramids"
  "Stratified design permits at most three layers per implementation namespace"]

 :spec/acceptance-criteria
 ["A deploy without an active :effect/deploy grant runs no kubectl mutation"
  "A mismatched or expired deploy grant runs no kubectl mutation"
  "check-resource-count denies a kustomize render exceeding :max-resources, before the real apply"
  "check-gke-node-limit denies a render exceeding :max-nodes, or is explicitly scoped away from the kustomize path with a replacement check that denies"
  "Each check remaining in the preflight path has a test asserting a violation over a kustomize render, not only over Pulumi preview JSON"
  "A preflight denial reports :deploy/stage :preflight, distinct from an authority failure"
  "(:dry-run! provider) is callable with the single argument transact! passes it"
  "A provider apply failure records :effect/outcome :failed in the durable effect store"
  "The manifest bytes in the durable proposal are byte-identical to those passed to the real apply"
  "The durable deploy proposal contains the provider dry-run diff"
  "A valid deploy records effect, grant, and DecisionEnvelope identifiers before mutation"
  ":evidence/rollback-info remains in context after a failed apply"
  "Reconciliation records the provider-observed deployment outcome"
  "poly check reports 0 errors and 0 warnings"
  "full bb test is green"]

 :spec/priority
 {:tier :high
  :axes #{:correctness :observation :governance-credibility}
  :theme :ariadne-grants
  :rationale "Deployment remains an ambient-authority escape hatch until mutation is proposed, granted, committed, and reconciled. The reused preflight checks cannot deny a kustomize render, so wiring the seam as-is would record a governance decision that was never made."
  :blocks []
  :blocked-by ["ariadne-grant-issuance.spec.edn"
               "ariadne-effect-transaction-fencing.spec.edn"]}

 :spec/workflow-type :canonical-sdlc}
